 and  listen to my gut and launch it cosmetics  uh in my living room um but drew and  i know you know this from being a huge  boss  that you are launching a business is  so much harder than i could have ever  imagined and  i didn't know that it would be three  years before i could  afford to pay myself in three years of  every beauty expert telling me no  um that it that the the this company  would never make it and you know drew i  had this vision to put real women as  models and try to  shift culture and beauty um and all the  big  all the big department stores and beauty  retailers everyone everyone said no so  it was  three years of constant rejection  so it was a tough start and you yourself  had gone through a personal experience  of feeling  rejected yourself which is why you  wanted  the women in your campaign to look a  certain way can you tell me about that  um drew one time we were a couple years  into our business and  i didn't know how we were going to make  it we were down to under a thousand  dollars  and in my personal account and company  count combined  and i got a big call from a potential  investor um  and it's like a huge private equity  company and they loved our product and  they've made a lot of products we shot  that in the grocery store really  famous household names and i thought it  was gonna be my big break and we went  through all these meetings  and we got down to the final meeting and  i flew up for the meeting he was  standing about three feet from me  and he said it's a no we're gonna  pass on investing in it cosmetics i just  don't think women  will buy makeup from someone who looks  like you with your body  and your weight and i remember  i felt like this lifetime of bodied out  and self-doubt fled my body  i went into my car and cried my eyes out  and this feeling in the  pit of my gut said he's wrong and i just  felt it and i also never got mad because  i realized oh he's just like the rest of  us he's been impacted  by the beauty industry too but he thinks  you have to look a certain way  to be successful and six years later um  when l'oreal bought it cosmetics and it  made the press everywhere  for 1.2 billion go ahead  he i heard from him that day he said  congratulations i'm so happy for you  i was wrong and i learned it would have  been the most successful  investment in his company's history and  like drew  had he believed in me back then when i  was so desperate i probably would have  given him the majority of the company  for almost no money but by the time we  sold  the business i was still the largest  shareholder so i was like thank god he  didn't believe in me  and sometimes our hardships and our  setbacks and they  they are painful and they're unfair and  they don't make sense but  i just think that um when we keep  believing in the possibility of our own  dreams and hearing our gut and believing  our setbacks are our setups  and i think all things are possible so  well i um i'm glad you don't  approach that uh with an angry you know  reception i think your high road  you know approach to being able to hear  that and have the lesson learned that  you should stick with your gut instinct  is fantastic  i want to take out all my anger issues  on this man but you know i'm glad he  called and said congratulations it  took the sting out of it a little bit  for me but  yeah you know i have watched the  trajectory of it cosmetics  as someone who's living inside the  beauty business and  it's just incredible you started this to  help people  to solve a problem i i  love your products too i mean they're  just that they're they're successful for  a reason they're really  gold standard in the industry and  everybody's on the feeder of it  cosmetics as they should be  and jamie the fact that you're sharing  your story which is just  especially when you're in like a beauty  industry or like a hollywood game it's  got to be  about who we are inside and  what our journey is and the outside is  affected by that  it's not the other way in how we look  and then that's the journey  it's in here and believe it how to go  from being underestimated to unstoppable  is available now wherever books are sold  100  of the proceeds are going to feeding  america  my goodness what an amazing person you  are thank you so much  thank you thank you thank you so much  [Music]

